1
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:48,970
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:51,900
[Episode 20]

3
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,250
Why are you here?

4
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,250
Do you think

5
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:41,520
you're so great?

6
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:47,430
Three million.

7
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:54,630
You paid back 3 million by yourself
over these 5 years.

8
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,500
Disappearing without a word—

9
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:00,270
what did you take us for?

10
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:07,200
This is my own business.

11
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,560
I can handle it.

12
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:10,870
You handle it?

13
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,560
You just lock yourself up here every day,

14
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,590
working day and night,

15
00:03:15,590 --> 00:03:16,840
gritting your teeth,

16
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:18,520
and refusing help from others.

17
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,400
Is this your way of handling it?

18
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,840
You are so stupid, Jiang Yubai!

19
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,150
If you hadn't disappeared,

20
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,540
and you had trusted us,

21
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,520
even if you had to work to make money,

22
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,000
we could have helped you.

23
00:03:40,079 --> 00:03:42,030
Duan Qiyan
could have helped you find clients,

24
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:43,990
Tang Tingting
could have helped you with promotion,

25
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:46,720
and Jin Baihui
could have helped you with design.

26
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:48,710
At least you wouldn't have to be

27
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:50,710
so tired and lonely all by yourself.

28
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:55,190
We wouldn't have to worry every day about

29
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,840
where you were

30
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,100
and how you were doing.

31
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,680
You could have even gone to school.

32
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,190
These 5 years

33
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,630
wouldn't have to be like this.

34
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:17,430
But you made
the most selfish and stupid choice.

35
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:25,160
Do you think you protected everyone
by doing this?

36
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,430
You didn't.

37
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,390
Other than

38
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:30,830
your own little ego,

39
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:32,190
you protected nothing.

40
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:34,130
You hurt all of us,

41
00:04:34,159 --> 00:04:35,420
especially yourself.

42
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:37,159
You hurt our friendship,

43
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:38,240
wasted your talent,

44
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:40,750
and gave up many better possibilities
for yourself!

45
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,480
Jiang Yubai, you big fool!

46
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:45,800
You are really stupid.

47
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,310
Lin Zhixia.

48
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:52,710
It's been five years—

49
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:56,100
more than a thousand days and nights.

50
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:58,409
I wish I could explain it

51
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:00,810
in a few words like you do.

52
00:05:01,890 --> 00:05:04,090
Of course I wanted to protect everyone.

53
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,740
But this is all I'm capable of.

54
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:16,110
But you shouldn't have run away.

55
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,000
You shouldn't have buried your head

56
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,530
in the sand like an ostrich.

57
00:05:20,310 --> 00:05:21,680
That was too selfish.

58
00:05:25,430 --> 00:05:26,160
Yeah.

59
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:29,870
I'm stupid

60
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,770
and selfish.

61
00:05:35,190 --> 00:05:36,360
I’m an idiot.

62
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:42,480
You've seen

63
00:05:44,909 --> 00:05:46,159
right through me.

64
00:05:57,159 --> 00:05:57,950
Then what...

65
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,750
are you going to do next?

66
00:06:11,190 --> 00:06:13,190
I can't just throw away

67
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:16,230
my worthless ego.

68
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:20,760
Otherwise, what do I have to hold on to?

69
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:33,510
I will try to reply to your messages.

70
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:40,090
Just give me some time.

71
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,240
I won't repeat

72
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,920
the importance of this project.

73
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:05,360
So for the overall success of the project,

74
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,800
and to ensure we don't waste anyone's

75
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:08,260
precious time and energy,

76
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:11,130
I have discussed it with the department.

77
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:14,040
Now we need to make
some necessary optimizations.

78
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,750
Please don't let it be me.

79
00:07:15,750 --> 00:07:18,310
I'm counting on this project
to help me find a job.

80
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,120
A job?

81
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:20,430
I'm struggling just to graduate.

82
00:07:20,430 --> 00:07:21,680
The list is out.

83
00:07:24,270 --> 00:07:25,070
Shasha.

84
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:26,800
Lu Ping.

85
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:29,310
That was close.

86
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,300
That's awful.

87
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:34,500
What are they going to do
about their graduation project?

88
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,270
Actually, the department
is also in a difficult position.

89
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:40,200
Forcing you to stay in this project

90
00:07:40,409 --> 00:07:42,570
would be torture for you

91
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:45,190
and irresponsible for the project.

92
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,070
So,

93
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:49,080
I will try my best...

94
00:07:49,310 --> 00:07:51,120
I can only say that I'll try my best

95
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,510
to communicate with teachers
of other projects

96
00:07:52,510 --> 00:07:53,120
and see

97
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,680
if we can transfer you
to a more suitable research group

98
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,940
that can better utilize your strengths.

99
00:07:58,890 --> 00:07:59,890
Did you hear that?

100
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,840
Kicking you two out is for your own good.

101
00:08:07,390 --> 00:08:08,850
As for the other students,

102
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:12,390
you must also be mentally prepared
for this.

103
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,950
Don't let it all be for nothing
in the end.

104
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,240
[Experimental Center, School of Mathematical Sciences,
Qingbei University]

105
00:08:18,950 --> 00:08:21,120
Keeping everyone
in their most suitable position

106
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,550
is being the most responsible
for the project

107
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:26,350
and the greatest protection
for them personally.

108
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,240
Am I wrong?

109
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:31,420
It's a deal then.

110
00:08:33,049 --> 00:08:33,740
Luo Ying.

111
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,960
What did you mean just now?

112
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:44,530
In front of everyone,

113
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,620
you embarrassed and undermined me.

114
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,900
I just couldn't stand you bullying others.

115
00:08:50,290 --> 00:08:51,890
Relying on your seniority and the project,

116
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:53,290
you treat students as consumables

117
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:55,290
and throw them away
when you're done using them.

118
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:56,050
Tan Qianche,

119
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:58,500
your extreme utilitarian methods

120
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,760
are truly disgusting.

121
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:05,650
Scientific research competition
is just this cruel.

122
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:06,860
I only want results.

123
00:09:06,940 --> 00:09:07,740
Yes,

124
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:10,630
you want your results
and your performance.

125
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,890
But when we voted earlier,

126
00:09:11,890 --> 00:09:13,700
pulling this on Lin Zhixia

127
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:15,450
was really unnecessary.

128
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:20,790
Don't think everyone
can't see your little schemes.

129
00:09:21,050 --> 00:09:23,180
You just want to be an academic tyrant,

130
00:09:23,370 --> 00:09:25,830
turning the lab
into your own dictatorship,

131
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:28,580
where those who submit thrive
and those who resist perish.

132
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:30,370
You squeeze the value
out of the useful ones

133
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:32,100
and kick away the useless ones.

134
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,130
All resources must revolve around you,

135
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:37,460
and all achievements must bear your name.

136
00:09:37,530 --> 00:09:38,770
Zhixia is just another person

137
00:09:38,770 --> 00:09:40,370
who refused to bow to you,

138
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,930
so you targeted her like this.

139
00:09:49,230 --> 00:09:51,090
Where those who submit thrive...

140
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:52,740
Exactly.

141
00:09:53,170 --> 00:09:54,890
Those who
follow the right research direction

142
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:56,220
and produce efficiently

143
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,080
should receive the most support.

144
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,530
This isn't being an academic tyrant.

145
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:03,530
This is basic efficiency
and survival of the fittest.

146
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:05,960
Stop glorifying yourself, Tan Qianche.

147
00:10:06,410 --> 00:10:08,650
Don't think everyone is like you.

148
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:11,220
At least Lin Zhixia isn't.

149
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:12,620
Also,

150
00:10:13,220 --> 00:10:15,820
we don't need to talk
when we meet in the future.

151
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:18,000
I can't keep up with your efficiency.

152
00:10:19,290 --> 00:10:20,290
From now on,

153
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:24,430
I'm also quitting your research group.

154
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:52,580
Thank you.

155
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:21,910
[Photos and Videos]

156
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,780
[Sending]

157
00:11:23,810 --> 00:11:24,830
[Photos and Videos]

158
00:11:24,990 --> 00:11:27,850
[Class Break]

159
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:31,860
Being away from home for years,

160
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,890
I don't even know
how to buy a bottle of water anymore.

161
00:11:33,890 --> 00:11:35,750
How on earth do you use this thing?

162
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:41,580
What? You're back?

163
00:11:42,250 --> 00:11:43,340
Did you manage to get some water?

164
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:44,500
Do you need me to transfer some money?

165
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,970
Don't die of thirst.

166
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:51,240
Dr. Shen has returned from his studies

167
00:11:51,240 --> 00:11:52,690
to contribute to his hometown.

168
00:11:52,690 --> 00:11:53,530
Welcome back!

169
00:11:58,990 --> 00:12:00,850
I still have some paperwork to do.

170
00:12:01,410 --> 00:12:03,130
Once I settle down
in the next couple of days,

171
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:05,100
let's grab a bite together.

172
00:12:35,170 --> 00:12:37,500
What did the Academic Affairs Office say?

173
00:12:40,410 --> 00:12:42,130
I'm doomed.

174
00:12:42,890 --> 00:12:44,890
I delayed my graduation for 2 years.

175
00:12:44,890 --> 00:12:47,550
My credits and research results
are not enough.

176
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:50,100
And there is no suitable project
this year.

177
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:52,780
Basically...

178
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:55,630
Basically,
I'll just leave without a degree.

179
00:12:58,770 --> 00:13:00,030
Are you satisfied now?

180
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:03,190
It's all because of your vote.

181
00:13:04,940 --> 00:13:06,940
It's useless to talk about this now.

182
00:13:07,650 --> 00:13:09,000
For the project I'm leading,

183
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,170
if you're willing,

184
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,790
I hope you can come and help me.

185
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:14,410
Help you, Lin Zhixia?

186
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:17,070
You're trying to kill me, aren't you?

187
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:20,010
Look at the workload of this project

188
00:13:20,460 --> 00:13:21,410
and its difficulty.

189
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,170
With just the two of us,

190
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:24,170
we won't finish it
even when I leave without a degree.

191
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:25,620
What's the use of me joining?

192
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,890
It's still a dead end.

193
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,340
Is there a difference?

194
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,200
Although there are only two of us,

195
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:33,880
-these data modules...
-Who said there are only two of you?

196
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:37,460
How can you leave us out

197
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,940
of such an interesting project?

198
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,650
I can take charge of data processing

199
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:42,010
and visualization.

200
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,810
I've practiced a lot recently.

201
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:47,890
For algorithm optimization
and simulation tests,

202
00:13:47,890 --> 00:13:48,890
I can give it a try.

203
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,700
Aren't you in Tan Qianche's group?

204
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,300
Don't talk nonsense.

205
00:13:53,650 --> 00:13:55,380
We have broken ties
with that academic tyrant

206
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,910
and come to join Lin Zhixia.

207
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:01,270
Do you have some confidence now,
Yang Shuwen?

208
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:04,000
It's not just the two of you now.

209
00:14:05,170 --> 00:14:06,620
It's a group of us.

210
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:10,110
Welcome, new team members.

211
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:20,340
Shen.

212
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:22,170
You just arrived,

213
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:24,860
so get familiar with the environment
as soon as possible.

214
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:27,250
This is the post-transplant
observation area.

215
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:28,890
It has strict sterile requirements.

216
00:14:28,890 --> 00:14:29,890
Hello, Director.

217
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:33,020
These are the regular chemotherapy wards.

218
00:14:33,290 --> 00:14:34,740
They have a high patient turnover.

219
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:37,050
Unlike other departments,

220
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:40,630
the patients we admit
all have complicated conditions.

221
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:42,220
I see.

222
00:14:42,370 --> 00:14:44,410
I'll get familiar with the patients' conditions
as soon as possible.

223
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:46,340
Look, we've got everything here. Let's go.

224
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,070
I won't do a bone marrow biopsy!

225
00:14:48,410 --> 00:14:49,170
Shui, don't be like this.

226
00:14:49,170 --> 00:14:50,170
Calm down.

227
00:14:50,410 --> 00:14:52,200
I won't do it! I won't do it!

228
00:14:52,650 --> 00:14:54,050
-Shui, don't be like this. Calm down.
-I won't do it!

229
00:14:54,050 --> 00:14:56,220
I won't do it. I said I won't!

230
00:14:56,370 --> 00:14:58,770
-I don't want to do it anymore!
-Bed 5, Shui.

231
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,630
Acute promyelocytic leukemia.

232
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:04,530
All plans have failed.

233
00:15:05,940 --> 00:15:07,340
Her bone marrow is a mess.

234
00:15:08,890 --> 00:15:09,770
Currently,

235
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,280
there is no good solution.

236
00:15:16,630 --> 00:15:18,230
It's mainly palliative care

237
00:15:18,510 --> 00:15:20,370
with some necessary monitoring.

238
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:23,200
Her family

239
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:26,030
wants her to suffer less.

240
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:36,820
Has she always been this resistant?

241
00:15:38,370 --> 00:15:39,410
Sometimes.

242
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:42,650
Shui.

243
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:43,980
I know

244
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:46,400
the treatment is very uncomfortable.

245
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,510
But look,

246
00:15:47,550 --> 00:15:49,950
your numbers are slowly improving, right?

247
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:52,630
You've been in the hospital for so long.

248
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:55,030
Don't you have a lot of things
you want to do?

249
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:57,980
Don't you want to be discharged earlier?

250
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:08,690
Then I'll only accept it

251
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:10,090
if he does it for me.

252
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,880
[Lin Zhixia]

253
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,730
Jiang Yubai,

254
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:08,369
I solved a big problem today.

255
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:10,500
Want to grab a meal together?

256
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:17,369
[Lin Zhixia]

257
00:17:18,619 --> 00:17:19,880
What do you want to eat?

258
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,250
Come find me first.

259
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:24,480
Let's decide together. How about that?

260
00:17:30,070 --> 00:17:30,740
Now?

261
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,060
The machines in my lab
are processing data.

262
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:37,640
I have nothing to do right now.

263
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,640
I'll wait for you.

264
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:44,750
See you downstairs at the lab in an hour.

265
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:47,080
Great.

266
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:09,380
This is Lab Building A.

267
00:18:11,030 --> 00:18:12,460
That is Lab Building B.

268
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:17,220
Isn't that the beautiful genius
from the Math Department?

269
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:18,220
Who is that guy?

270
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,250
What do you want to eat?

271
00:18:19,250 --> 00:18:20,400
Maybe it's her brother?

272
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,400
Anything is fine.

273
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:24,350
Let me think.

274
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:27,250
Good afternoon, Dr. Lin.

275
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,530
-Good afternoon.
-Senior.

276
00:18:28,530 --> 00:18:29,920
I figured out the algorithm
you explained last time.

277
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,010
You are amazing.

278
00:18:31,010 --> 00:18:31,810
That's great.

279
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:33,880
Feel free to ask me
if you have any questions.

280
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,080
We'll be leaving now.

281
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:35,920
Bye-bye.

282
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,310
Is that guy a school staff member?

283
00:18:38,310 --> 00:18:39,270
How did he get together with her?

284
00:18:39,270 --> 00:18:40,330
I know what to eat.

285
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,510
-Hello, Dr. Lin.
-Hello, Dr. Lin.

286
00:18:42,510 --> 00:18:44,240
Stir-fried beef in Canteen 3.

287
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,110
I can afford a meal.

288
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:50,190
You don't have to save money for me.

289
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:51,670
It's not about the money.

290
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:53,130
You have no idea,

291
00:18:53,130 --> 00:18:54,440
in Canteen 3 of our school,

292
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:56,100
there is a very popular stall.

293
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:58,510
The stir-fried beef
is the chef's specialty,

294
00:18:58,510 --> 00:19:00,590
perfectly cooked and in limited supply.

295
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:01,590
I've been here for 5 years,

296
00:19:01,590 --> 00:19:03,390
and I've never managed to get it.

297
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:06,500
So, are you confident we'll get it today?

298
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:11,270
Okay.

299
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,940
It's not peak dining time
right now anyway.

300
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:14,920
Let's go now.

301
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:16,270
Let's go.

302
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:19,590
Hurry up!

303
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:25,160
Senior.

304
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:28,550
Senior, finally I found you.

305
00:19:28,550 --> 00:19:29,250
Help me.

306
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:30,390
What's wrong?

307
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,480
We were researching

308
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,640
an optimization problem this afternoon
and got stuck.

309
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:35,550
We went to the lab just now
and they said you weren't there.

310
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:36,950
Here. Please take a look.

311
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:39,680
You guys talk.

312
00:19:40,090 --> 00:19:41,220
I'll go buy the food.

313
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:44,450
It's like this.

314
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:46,940
Suppose we have a non-convex,
high-dimensional energy

315
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:49,590
embedding mapping of molecular
and atomic coordinates.

316
00:19:49,590 --> 00:19:51,240
It does not meet the requirements
of the objective function.

317
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:52,830
Please help us analyze this

318
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:54,630
and figure out what we should do.

319
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,720
You can use
the accelerated gradient method.

320
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,440
Ma'am, I want this and this.

321
00:20:00,550 --> 00:20:02,350
Ma'am, I want this and this.

322
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,820
Very detailed.

323
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:08,790
Thank you.

324
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:15,030
Ma'am, I want
2 portions of stir-fried beef.

325
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:15,750
And...

326
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:16,880
Stir-fried beef?

327
00:20:17,310 --> 00:20:18,240
It sold out long ago.

328
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,240
You came so late.

329
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,240
Are you new here?

330
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:22,790
Order something else, will you?

331
00:20:22,790 --> 00:20:23,590
Let me think.

332
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,200
Excuse me.

333
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Ma'am, I'll have a portion of tomatoes
and this one.

334
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:37,160
Hello, Jiang.

335
00:20:37,350 --> 00:20:38,070
I can't hear you.

336
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:38,720
Hello?

337
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,270
It's okay now.

338
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:42,070
Jiang, something bad happened.

339
00:20:42,070 --> 00:20:43,200
The old man from last time—

340
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,880
his speaker has a problem again.

341
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,000
He said the bass is still not good,

342
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,160
too boomy and muffled.

343
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,590
He also criticized
your modification skills.

344
00:20:48,590 --> 00:20:49,880
I've talked my head off,

345
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,030
but he is just not satisfied.

346
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:51,790
He's very angry.

347
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:55,070
Come on. I've modified it 3 times
according to his requests.

348
00:20:55,070 --> 00:20:56,030
Three times.

349
00:20:56,310 --> 00:20:58,090
The speaker is already at its limit.

350
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,310
It's the law of physics.

351
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:00,710
There's nothing I can do.

352
00:21:00,870 --> 00:21:01,880
Tell him this—

353
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,030
either use it as it is,

354
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:05,450
or just change the box.

355
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,440
I can't do anything about it.

356
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:07,400
My bro.

357
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,440
Master Jiang.

358
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:10,300
I don't dare to say that.

359
00:21:10,590 --> 00:21:12,270
This old man,
even though he's about to retire,

360
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:13,670
has a lot of connections.

361
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:16,140
Our little shop can't stand his nagging.

362
00:21:16,350 --> 00:21:18,240
He doesn't contribute much to our income,

363
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,880
but if he spreads
negative comments about us,

364
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,410
it could do serious damage.

365
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:23,310
The machine has already been sent back.

366
00:21:23,310 --> 00:21:25,570
Please think of a way as soon as possible.

367
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,410
Alright.

368
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,720
I'll check it tomorrow morning.

369
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:30,590
No, not tomorrow, bro.

370
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:31,750
Where are you now?

371
00:21:31,750 --> 00:21:33,640
The old man is losing his temper here,

372
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:34,880
saying if he doesn't hear
a satisfying sound tonight,

373
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:35,750
he won't sleep.

374
00:21:36,070 --> 00:21:37,790
If he doesn't sleep,
I can forget about sleeping too.

375
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:39,830
Jiang, I'm begging you.
Please help.

376
00:21:39,830 --> 00:21:40,760
Okay.

377
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,240
I got it.

378
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:49,310
Is it this one?

379
00:21:49,310 --> 00:21:51,880
Is the interval between 0 and 0.2?

380
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:52,790
It's...

381
00:21:53,030 --> 00:21:54,200
0.05.

382
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,400
-It’s all wrong.
-Yes.

383
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:56,110
Right?

384
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:57,880
Any other questions?

385
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:58,680
No.

386
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:00,790
Senior.

387
00:22:00,790 --> 00:22:02,110
The East China campus mixer

388
00:22:02,110 --> 00:22:03,480
has invited us twice.

389
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:04,400
Let's go together.

390
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,240
I think I'll pass.

391
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:06,920
You are the face of our math department.

392
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,650
You'll blow them away if you go.

393
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,270
I'll message you later.

394
00:22:10,870 --> 00:22:11,880
My friend is waiting for me.

395
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,570
I have to go.

396
00:22:13,110 --> 00:22:13,830
Bye.

397
00:22:13,830 --> 00:22:14,360
Bye-bye.

398
00:22:14,510 --> 00:22:15,400
Bye-bye.

399
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,200
Smells so good.

400
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:20,900
I'm sorry.

401
00:22:21,750 --> 00:22:23,070
I didn't get the beef.

402
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,350
It's fine. It's hard to get anyway.

403
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,040
These dishes are enough.

404
00:22:29,590 --> 00:22:30,400
Try this.

405
00:22:30,510 --> 00:22:31,960
It's really tender.

406
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:35,640
-Senior Lin.
-Senior Lin.

407
00:22:35,640 --> 00:22:37,160
We rarely see you in Canteen 3.

408
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,110
How come you have time today?

409
00:22:38,110 --> 00:22:38,830
Senior Lin,

410
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,070
may I have your WeChat?

411
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,140
I have so many questions for you.

412
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:51,610
Thank you.

413
00:22:52,110 --> 00:22:53,110
By the way, Senior Lin,

414
00:22:53,110 --> 00:22:54,160
about my paper...

415
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:55,890
How about I look at it on WeChat?

416
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:57,270
My friend is here.

417
00:22:58,720 --> 00:22:59,880
Okay.

418
00:22:59,880 --> 00:23:01,030
Thanks, Senior. No problem.

419
00:23:01,030 --> 00:23:01,790
Bye, Senior.

420
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:03,590
We'll keep in touch, Senior Lin.

421
00:23:08,250 --> 00:23:10,450
Don't worry about the beef.

422
00:23:10,590 --> 00:23:12,250
I just came here to try my luck.

423
00:23:13,010 --> 00:23:14,040
Lin Zhixia,

424
00:23:15,030 --> 00:23:15,960
I just...

425
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:18,200
Senior Lin?

426
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:19,310
I've heard so much about you.

427
00:23:19,310 --> 00:23:21,510
We can never register for your classes.

428
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:23,310
Come earlier next time.

429
00:23:23,310 --> 00:23:24,510
Okay. Thanks, Senior.

430
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:25,880
Bye-bye, Senior Sister.

431
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,070
She is Lin Zhixia?

432
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:27,960
Yes.

433
00:23:29,070 --> 00:23:30,400
I rarely come here.

434
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,110
I usually eat near the lab.

435
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:33,310
Try this.

436
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:41,880
I just remembered I...

437
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:44,030
have something urgent to handle.

438
00:23:44,030 --> 00:23:46,230
I'll spend more time with you next time.

439
00:23:46,790 --> 00:23:47,520
I'm leaving.

440
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,920
Jiang Yubai, wait.

441
00:24:01,110 --> 00:24:03,070
I'm sorry. I ruined your meal.

442
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,680
It's not that.

443
00:24:08,130 --> 00:24:09,330
It's my own business.

444
00:24:09,330 --> 00:24:10,260
I know.

445
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:11,960
I was talking to others

446
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:13,240
and left you hanging.

447
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:15,810
Don't overthink it.

448
00:24:16,590 --> 00:24:17,690
I really have something urgent.

449
00:24:17,690 --> 00:24:18,750
Then I'll go with you.

450
00:24:18,750 --> 00:24:19,240
No need.

451
00:24:25,270 --> 00:24:26,800
You don't need to see me off.

452
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:27,960
Go back.

453
00:24:29,030 --> 00:24:30,560
I'll come see you next time.

454
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:32,850
Are you mad?

455
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:48,700
No.

456
00:24:51,570 --> 00:24:52,830
You are doing well now.

457
00:24:54,290 --> 00:24:56,550
Your trajectory hasn't deviated at all.

458
00:24:57,070 --> 00:24:58,920
You are what you wanted to be.

459
00:25:00,850 --> 00:25:02,380
Of course I'm happy for you.

460
00:25:05,050 --> 00:25:05,780
It's just...

461
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:07,770
It's just that I am not at all the person

462
00:25:07,770 --> 00:25:08,750
I wanted to be.

463
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:13,900
This high-dimensional whatever,
this bullshit function stuff...

464
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:15,630
I don't understand a word of it.

465
00:25:16,110 --> 00:25:17,460
Every day, all I think about is

466
00:25:17,460 --> 00:25:19,520
how to solder the next circuit board,

467
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:21,420
how to deal with difficult clients,

468
00:25:21,420 --> 00:25:22,950
and how to save enough money

469
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:26,800
to pay off my debts.

470
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,380
Lin Zhixia, you know what?

471
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,890
For a moment, I suddenly felt like

472
00:25:35,330 --> 00:25:37,000
we don't live in the same world anymore.

473
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,320
Debts can be paid,

474
00:25:39,400 --> 00:25:40,700
and problems can be solved.

475
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:42,560
-There will be a way.
-Lin Zhixia.

476
00:25:44,310 --> 00:25:46,110
Let me think about it carefully.

477
00:25:46,590 --> 00:25:48,250
Let's talk another day, okay?

478
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:51,010
Are you going to hide again?

479
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,530
I just want to figure this out
by myself first.

480
00:25:57,660 --> 00:25:58,270
Alright?

481
00:26:07,310 --> 00:26:08,240
I'm leaving now.

482
00:26:49,380 --> 00:26:50,050
Hou Wei.

483
00:26:50,290 --> 00:26:52,570
We must get this guy.

484
00:26:52,940 --> 00:26:55,600
I pulled a lot of strings
to get in touch with him.

485
00:26:55,740 --> 00:26:58,250
He's the former chief architect
of Xunchi Travel.

486
00:26:58,250 --> 00:27:00,310
With him leading our tech iteration,

487
00:27:00,330 --> 00:27:01,900
our system will be saved.

488
00:27:01,980 --> 00:27:02,810
By then, the user experience

489
00:27:02,810 --> 00:27:04,410
will reach a whole new level.

490
00:27:04,770 --> 00:27:05,700
Duan.

491
00:27:05,940 --> 00:27:08,070
800,000. An annual salary of 800,000.

492
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:10,380
Have you checked how much money is left
in our account?

493
00:27:10,380 --> 00:27:12,250
We can barely pay our employees
next month.

494
00:27:12,250 --> 00:27:13,330
Let alone 800,000.

495
00:27:13,330 --> 00:27:15,390
I'd have to think twice about 80,000.

496
00:27:15,850 --> 00:27:18,140
This is what we call an investment.

497
00:27:18,500 --> 00:27:19,330
Right?

498
00:27:19,940 --> 00:27:22,460
If we don't lay a solid foundation
from the start,

499
00:27:22,460 --> 00:27:24,500
with constant bugs
and a terrible user experience,

500
00:27:24,500 --> 00:27:26,850
and users can't even unlock a bike
after trying twice in a single ride,

501
00:27:26,850 --> 00:27:28,380
who would use our bikes?

502
00:27:28,420 --> 00:27:31,050
No matter how much money we burn
on promotion,

503
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:32,570
it'll all be in vain.

504
00:27:32,570 --> 00:27:34,010
What is the most important thing?

505
00:27:34,010 --> 00:27:34,850
The most important thing is

506
00:27:34,850 --> 00:27:37,420
that we need to focus
on the product itself.

507
00:27:39,420 --> 00:27:41,950
Users don't have such high demands
right now.

508
00:27:42,140 --> 00:27:43,380
As long as it unlocks
and they can ride it,

509
00:27:43,380 --> 00:27:45,090
and it's cheap, that's enough.

510
00:27:45,090 --> 00:27:46,850
We are marking our territory now.

511
00:27:46,850 --> 00:27:48,380
It's a period of expansion.

512
00:27:49,010 --> 00:27:50,180
Fine.

513
00:27:50,660 --> 00:27:52,590
Don't hire him if you don't want to.

514
00:27:52,940 --> 00:27:53,940
We're not on the same page.

515
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:54,870
I'm going to eat.

516
00:27:55,890 --> 00:27:57,010
You...

517
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:04,110
[Xian's Restaurant]

518
00:28:12,220 --> 00:28:13,010
Welcome.

519
00:28:32,090 --> 00:28:33,330
Do you know
how many new bikes our competitors

520
00:28:33,330 --> 00:28:35,220
put into the city this month?

521
00:28:35,770 --> 00:28:37,770
We need to spend our money wisely.

522
00:28:38,180 --> 00:28:40,510
We have to flood the market
with our bikes,

523
00:28:40,700 --> 00:28:42,420
gain a foothold, and survive.

524
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:44,140
Then we'll talk about the rest.

525
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:44,980
Survive?

526
00:28:45,940 --> 00:28:48,500
How can you do that
with a bunch of junk?

527
00:28:48,610 --> 00:28:50,530
Hou Wei, you're drinking poison
to quench your thirst.

528
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:52,090
We still need to quench it first.

529
00:28:52,090 --> 00:28:53,750
If we die, we'll have nothing!

530
00:28:55,980 --> 00:28:56,570
Duan.

531
00:28:57,180 --> 00:28:59,290
Can you be a bit more realistic?

532
00:29:03,180 --> 00:29:03,980
Wait a moment.

533
00:29:14,220 --> 00:29:16,150
Hello, what would you like to have?

534
00:29:22,810 --> 00:29:24,330
Just a bowl of tonkotsu ramen.

535
00:29:24,330 --> 00:29:25,010
Thank you.

536
00:29:29,460 --> 00:29:30,980
The entire model is divided into

537
00:29:30,980 --> 00:29:33,050
4 sections: A, B, C, and D.

538
00:29:33,530 --> 00:29:34,980
Everyone has their own strengths.

539
00:29:34,980 --> 00:29:35,770
So,

540
00:29:35,620 --> 00:29:37,650
[Project Division]

541
00:29:35,900 --> 00:29:37,850
our coordination is crucial.

542
00:29:38,050 --> 00:29:39,450
Please look at this part.

543
00:29:40,290 --> 00:29:43,050
The convergence verification
of this module is very important.

544
00:29:40,410 --> 00:29:49,140
[Project Division]

545
00:29:43,380 --> 00:29:45,640
It is the foundation of our entire model.

546
00:29:46,220 --> 00:29:47,980
Shuwen, you have a solid math foundation.

547
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:48,980
You'll handle this part.

548
00:29:48,980 --> 00:29:50,460
I'm not confident about that.

549
00:29:50,460 --> 00:29:51,660
If I want to graduate this year,

550
00:29:51,660 --> 00:29:53,460
I still have to polish my thesis.

551
00:29:53,530 --> 00:29:54,380
What if...

552
00:29:54,610 --> 00:29:56,570
What if I don't allocate my energy well

553
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:58,050
and mess it up?

554
00:29:59,180 --> 00:30:00,940
Okay, I'll handle this part.

555
00:30:01,700 --> 00:30:03,180
You'll just work with Luo Ying

556
00:30:03,180 --> 00:30:05,090
to handle the data preprocessing.

557
00:30:05,090 --> 00:30:07,950
Make sure there are no issues
with the entire input.

558
00:30:08,530 --> 00:30:10,570
Shasha,
continue with the literature review.

559
00:30:10,570 --> 00:30:13,180
Focus on the Monte Carlo method

560
00:30:13,180 --> 00:30:15,090
and its latest application
to this problem.

561
00:30:15,090 --> 00:30:16,420
Compile a review for me.

562
00:30:17,220 --> 00:30:19,740
Lu Ping, for the code optimization
you're handling,

563
00:30:19,740 --> 00:30:21,500
give me a preliminary version
by tomorrow at the latest.

564
00:30:21,500 --> 00:30:22,230
Is that okay?

565
00:30:22,500 --> 00:30:23,290
Okay.

566
00:30:25,090 --> 00:30:26,620
Alright, let's get to work.

567
00:30:31,500 --> 00:30:32,140
Zhixia.

568
00:30:38,330 --> 00:30:39,260
This won't work.

569
00:30:39,940 --> 00:30:41,250
If you take all the core tasks
on yourself,

570
00:30:41,250 --> 00:30:42,450
you'll be exhausted.

571
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:48,020
Yang Shuwen is obviously
just drifting along.

572
00:30:52,940 --> 00:30:53,810
I know that.

573
00:30:54,530 --> 00:30:56,130
But there's nothing I can do.

574
00:30:56,290 --> 00:30:58,620
I have to make sure the project continues.

575
00:30:58,700 --> 00:31:00,900
At least we are moving forward now,

576
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:01,610
aren't we?

577
00:31:05,220 --> 00:31:05,850
Let's go.

578
00:31:19,070 --> 00:31:19,590
[Jiang Yubai]

579
00:31:19,610 --> 00:31:23,570
[What a nice day. What are you doing?]

580
00:31:34,990 --> 00:31:41,520
[Lin Zhixia]

581
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:38,420
What a nice day.

582
00:31:39,180 --> 00:31:40,290
What are you doing?

583
00:31:53,750 --> 00:31:58,670
[Repayment Plan for the Next 3 Months]

584
00:32:08,610 --> 00:32:09,610
How does it taste?

585
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:10,790
Is it to your liking?

586
00:32:12,290 --> 00:32:14,010
To be honest,

587
00:32:14,740 --> 00:32:17,700
it's delicious. The broth is so authentic.

588
00:32:18,700 --> 00:32:21,140
Thank you. I'm glad you like it.

589
00:32:21,860 --> 00:32:23,460
Are you usually around here?

590
00:32:24,410 --> 00:32:26,470
Yes, our company is not far from here.

591
00:32:27,050 --> 00:32:28,850
But how come I didn't know

592
00:32:28,850 --> 00:32:31,710
there was such a delicious noodle shop
around here?

593
00:32:33,740 --> 00:32:35,140
This is our ordering card.

594
00:32:35,140 --> 00:32:36,940
It has our phone number and menu.

595
00:32:37,090 --> 00:32:39,150
Contact us anytime you want to order.

596
00:32:40,090 --> 00:32:40,850
Okay.

597
00:32:41,220 --> 00:32:42,220
I will come often.

598
00:32:44,380 --> 00:32:45,180
Engineer Xie.

599
00:32:45,330 --> 00:32:46,330
This is our research group's

600
00:32:46,330 --> 00:32:48,640
computing power requirement form
for next quarter.

601
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:49,840
Sorry to trouble you.

602
00:32:50,160 --> 00:32:51,690
Please arrange it this way.

603
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:53,740
Dr. Tan.

604
00:32:54,610 --> 00:32:55,500
You have...

605
00:32:55,770 --> 00:32:58,570
taken up almost all

606
00:32:58,570 --> 00:33:00,110
the golden computing hours.

607
00:33:00,110 --> 00:33:01,250
Other projects,

608
00:33:01,570 --> 00:33:03,530
especially those requiring

609
00:33:03,610 --> 00:33:05,270
long continuous simulation,

610
00:33:05,700 --> 00:33:08,660
have been pushed
to early morning and weekends.

611
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:11,610
And the duration
has been greatly compressed.

612
00:33:11,610 --> 00:33:13,010
This might not be enough.

613
00:33:14,510 --> 00:33:16,370
And Dr. Lin Zhixia

614
00:33:16,830 --> 00:33:19,360
also submitted
a detailed application to me.

615
00:33:19,810 --> 00:33:22,870
Her project has quite high
computational complexity.

616
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,730
If we follow your arrangement,

617
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:27,530
the resources left for her
will not be enough.

618
00:33:27,750 --> 00:33:28,810
I understand

619
00:33:29,110 --> 00:33:29,910
what you mean.

620
00:33:30,940 --> 00:33:32,540
But my project is different.

621
00:33:32,810 --> 00:33:34,440
It is a key project supported
by the department this year,

622
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:35,420
with a clear requirement to produce

623
00:33:35,420 --> 00:33:36,660
landmark results.

624
00:33:36,980 --> 00:33:37,790
So all resources should naturally

625
00:33:37,790 --> 00:33:39,350
be directed toward the area
that best demonstrates

626
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:41,660
our department's research capabilities.

627
00:33:41,660 --> 00:33:42,570
Am I right?

628
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:45,090
That may be true,

629
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:46,770
but what about Dr. Lin?

630
00:33:46,770 --> 00:33:47,570
Engineer Xie,

631
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:51,610
let's be honest here.

632
00:33:52,540 --> 00:33:54,800
Who are the people with Dr. Lin right now?

633
00:33:55,790 --> 00:33:57,960
Yang Shuwen, whose graduation
was delayed for 2 years,

634
00:33:57,960 --> 00:33:59,810
Deng Shasha, and Lu Ping,

635
00:33:59,810 --> 00:34:01,640
who were just let go from my team.

636
00:34:03,930 --> 00:34:05,590
Actually, for some projects,

637
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:07,110
their meaning of existence

638
00:34:07,110 --> 00:34:09,710
is not about
how many results they can produce,

639
00:34:09,739 --> 00:34:12,469
but rather to provide a place
for certain people.

640
00:34:13,250 --> 00:34:14,780
You know what I mean, right?

641
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:19,820
Fine.

642
00:34:20,389 --> 00:34:21,210
I got it.

643
00:34:21,940 --> 00:34:23,070
We'll do it your way.

644
00:34:24,090 --> 00:34:24,690
Thank you.

645
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:36,880
Master Jiang, it's me,

646
00:35:36,970 --> 00:35:37,630
Cheng.

647
00:35:40,050 --> 00:35:40,600
Coming.

648
00:35:47,200 --> 00:35:48,030
Master Jiang,

649
00:35:48,190 --> 00:35:49,170
great news.

650
00:35:49,420 --> 00:35:50,600
I got you a big order.

651
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:52,420
Enough to feed you for 3 months.

652
00:35:52,530 --> 00:35:55,530
It will definitely update
your long vacation plan again.

653
00:35:55,530 --> 00:35:56,170
Tell me.

654
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:58,660
It's a customized order.

655
00:35:59,130 --> 00:36:00,930
The requirements are very high.

656
00:36:01,630 --> 00:36:02,460
But

657
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:04,630
the pay is definitely worth it.

658
00:36:06,190 --> 00:36:08,440
It's just that
they have a special request.

659
00:36:08,440 --> 00:36:10,670
The finished product
cannot have any of your marks,

660
00:36:10,670 --> 00:36:12,420
logos, signatures, or anything—

661
00:36:12,420 --> 00:36:13,210
none of them.

662
00:36:16,460 --> 00:36:17,780
Cannot have my mark?

663
00:36:18,500 --> 00:36:19,630
What does that mean?

664
00:36:20,570 --> 00:36:21,840
Take my stuff

665
00:36:22,010 --> 00:36:23,410
and put their brand on it?

666
00:36:23,950 --> 00:36:25,160
You think too much.

667
00:36:25,330 --> 00:36:27,880
They are not doing business
or making knock-offs.

668
00:36:27,880 --> 00:36:29,670
Just a bunch of rich kids
playing with cars.

669
00:36:29,670 --> 00:36:31,210
They want a batch of unique car stereos

670
00:36:31,210 --> 00:36:33,480
that can't be bought on the market.

671
00:36:33,690 --> 00:36:35,690
Just to show off, pure private toys.

672
00:36:39,300 --> 00:36:41,730
I guarantee it
with your next month's rent.

673
00:36:49,130 --> 00:36:49,940
Cheng,

674
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:53,380
there are only 2 ways out for my stuff.

675
00:36:54,230 --> 00:36:56,730
Either bear my mark proudly,

676
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:58,690
or rot in the warehouse.

677
00:37:00,730 --> 00:37:03,130
Want me to be a ghost technician
for others?

678
00:37:03,690 --> 00:37:04,420
No way.

679
00:37:05,380 --> 00:37:06,570
Bro, Brother Jiang.

680
00:37:06,590 --> 00:37:08,190
It's really not rebranding.

681
00:37:08,300 --> 00:37:10,280
It will never flow into the market.

682
00:37:11,460 --> 00:37:13,960
It's just a bunch of
vain young masters and misses.

683
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:15,500
They want something unique

684
00:37:15,500 --> 00:37:17,620
and mysterious
that they can't tell the origin of.

685
00:37:17,620 --> 00:37:20,150
I guarantee
it won't damage your reputation.

686
00:37:20,730 --> 00:37:21,650
Besides,

687
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:23,670
this order is very profitable,

688
00:37:24,690 --> 00:37:26,620
and it can solve your urgent needs.

689
00:37:30,150 --> 00:37:34,590
[Repayment Plan for the Next 3 Months]

690
00:38:11,210 --> 00:38:13,180
[Mom]

691
00:38:12,570 --> 00:38:15,170
Jin Baihui, what is wrong with you?

692
00:38:15,350 --> 00:38:16,880
Li Zhe is such a great catch.

693
00:38:17,190 --> 00:38:18,630
Why aren't you interested in him?

694
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:20,160
I came with you to Huacheng.

695
00:38:20,690 --> 00:38:22,400
Your dad worked hard for so many years

696
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:23,500
and didn't even take
the division director position.

697
00:38:23,500 --> 00:38:25,420
He took a half-rank demotion to come here,

698
00:38:25,420 --> 00:38:26,680
all for you.

699
00:38:27,340 --> 00:38:28,610
What are we doing this for?

700
00:38:28,610 --> 00:38:30,200
Tell me, what are we doing this for?

701
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:32,250
Don't we just want you
to have a good life?

702
00:38:32,250 --> 00:38:33,780
Marrying well at your age

703
00:38:33,780 --> 00:38:35,730
is 100 times better
than working hard in the future.

704
00:38:35,730 --> 00:38:36,340
Why...

705
00:38:35,950 --> 00:38:36,640
[Mom]

706
00:38:36,630 --> 00:38:38,260
Why can't you just understand?

707
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:40,970
[Back then, didn't I...]

708
00:39:20,130 --> 00:39:20,940
Dr. Lin.

709
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,010
Engineer Jin?

710
00:39:24,450 --> 00:39:25,650
What brings you here?

711
00:39:26,320 --> 00:39:27,690
I knew you have been working hard
and forgot to eat,

712
00:39:27,690 --> 00:39:29,190
so I brought you some snacks.

713
00:39:29,190 --> 00:39:30,170
Great.

714
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:31,590
Let me see what it is.

715
00:39:33,530 --> 00:39:34,690
Smells so good.

716
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:41,010
I came out to get some fresh air too.

717
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:44,040
What did your mom do this time?

718
00:39:45,840 --> 00:39:46,570
The usual.

719
00:39:48,670 --> 00:39:51,200
It seems all mothers in the world
are the same.

720
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:53,940
If I had a mom like yours,

721
00:39:54,460 --> 00:39:56,460
I'd wake up laughing from my dreams.

722
00:39:57,670 --> 00:40:00,730
My mom has been complaining
in the group chat every day.

723
00:40:00,730 --> 00:40:02,460
What is she complaining about?

724
00:40:03,090 --> 00:40:03,900
My brother.

725
00:40:05,670 --> 00:40:06,470
Your brother?

726
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:08,290
What's wrong with him?

727
00:40:09,090 --> 00:40:10,890
She keeps pushing him
to get a girlfriend every day.

728
00:40:10,890 --> 00:40:13,130
She sends him WeChat messages
every now and then

729
00:40:13,130 --> 00:40:14,460
with a bunch of

730
00:40:14,460 --> 00:40:16,650
matchmaking accounts.

731
00:40:16,670 --> 00:40:18,680
He is so annoyed.

732
00:40:19,690 --> 00:40:21,690
Elders are all pretty much the same.

733
00:40:24,070 --> 00:40:27,070
Doesn't your brother have any thoughts
on it himself?

734
00:40:27,190 --> 00:40:28,260
What thoughts could he have?

735
00:40:28,260 --> 00:40:29,660
He's like a block of wood.

736
00:40:29,690 --> 00:40:32,030
His girlfriend is code and game consoles.

737
00:40:33,380 --> 00:40:35,980
But my brother is actually quite obedient.

738
00:40:36,590 --> 00:40:38,390
He should be compromising soon.

739
00:40:43,590 --> 00:40:44,260
Oh, right.

740
00:40:47,670 --> 00:40:48,460
Take this.

741
00:40:49,300 --> 00:40:50,170
So much?

742
00:40:50,190 --> 00:40:51,380
I can't finish it all.

743
00:40:51,380 --> 00:40:52,380
It's from our department.

744
00:40:52,380 --> 00:40:53,570
I still have some in my dorm.

745
00:40:53,570 --> 00:40:55,500
Just think of it as helping me out.

746
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:58,940
Thank you. I'll gladly accept it.

747
00:41:00,230 --> 00:41:01,650
This is delicious.

748
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:02,840
Where did you buy it?

749
00:41:03,170 --> 00:41:04,050
It's very popular recently.

750
00:41:04,050 --> 00:41:05,380
I saw it on the internet.

751
00:41:06,090 --> 00:41:07,750
There's also sausage flavor?

752
00:41:09,920 --> 00:41:10,860
So many nuts.

753
00:41:11,900 --> 00:41:13,100
Let me taste this one.

754
00:41:21,110 --> 00:41:27,000
[Star Shine Media]

755
00:41:27,570 --> 00:41:29,760
Su Mo's performance has been good lately.

756
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:31,170
He's got great momentum.

757
00:41:32,510 --> 00:41:34,510
You deserve a lot of credit for this.

758
00:41:34,820 --> 00:41:37,010
Although you haven't
been in the industry long,

759
00:41:37,010 --> 00:41:39,340
you're really good at guiding newcomers.

760
00:41:39,510 --> 00:41:41,570
It's impressive you've done so well.

761
00:41:42,030 --> 00:41:43,030
Thank you, Mr. Li.

762
00:41:44,010 --> 00:41:45,570
I came here today to see

763
00:41:45,570 --> 00:41:47,340
if the company could give Su Mo

764
00:41:47,340 --> 00:41:48,460
more resources.

765
00:41:49,260 --> 00:41:52,060
I think he will definitely
seize the opportunity.

766
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:59,500
I've been thinking lately about

767
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:01,090
how I can help you.

768
00:42:02,070 --> 00:42:03,170
With your abilities,

769
00:42:03,170 --> 00:42:05,530
you can definitely join a better team.

770
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:09,000
You can only show your strengths
with more resources.

771
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:09,960
Right?

772
00:42:11,530 --> 00:42:14,460
Bingbing has been
working on a lot of scripts lately.

773
00:42:15,210 --> 00:42:16,900
Her team is a bit overwhelmed.

774
00:42:17,610 --> 00:42:20,210
Have you thought about
going over to help them?

775
00:42:20,210 --> 00:42:22,420
You mean helping to read scripts?

776
00:42:24,670 --> 00:42:27,870
I want you to go over and be Bingbing's
executive manager.

777
00:42:29,260 --> 00:42:30,460
I've talked to her about it,

778
00:42:30,460 --> 00:42:31,320
and she agreed.

779
00:42:31,710 --> 00:42:33,310
This is a great opportunity.

780
00:42:33,820 --> 00:42:35,280
Do you want to give it a try?

781
00:42:37,380 --> 00:42:38,860
If I go over,

782
00:42:39,090 --> 00:42:40,500
can I still manage Su Mo?

783
00:42:42,070 --> 00:42:43,010
Bingbing

784
00:42:43,170 --> 00:42:44,940
definitely wants her team

785
00:42:44,940 --> 00:42:46,420
to focus on her work.

786
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:49,400
And you know Bingbing's personality.

787
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,860
As long as you do a good job,

788
00:42:50,900 --> 00:42:52,430
she won't treat you poorly.

789
00:42:57,030 --> 00:42:58,960
Mr. Li, I understand what you mean.

790
00:42:59,210 --> 00:43:00,980
Can you give me some time

791
00:43:00,980 --> 00:43:01,980
to think about it?

792
00:43:03,210 --> 00:43:03,900
Sure.

793
00:43:04,570 --> 00:43:06,300
Anyway, that's the situation.

794
00:43:06,670 --> 00:43:09,200
Let me know
whenever you've made up your mind.

795
00:43:09,690 --> 00:43:11,690
Okay, thank you. I'll head out now.

796
00:43:11,690 --> 00:43:12,380
Okay.

797
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:27,140
[Server Room]

798
00:43:28,510 --> 00:43:31,040
Just leave the takeout at the door.
Thank you.

799
00:43:31,510 --> 00:43:32,420
It's me.

800
00:43:34,580 --> 00:43:35,340
Hi.

801
00:43:36,630 --> 00:43:37,820
What brings you here?

802
00:43:37,820 --> 00:43:39,860
Lin Zhixia asked me
to bring you something.

803
00:43:39,860 --> 00:43:41,090
She said you've been staying up late,

804
00:43:41,090 --> 00:43:42,900
so she wanted you to get some nutrition.

805
00:43:42,900 --> 00:43:44,730
She could've just sent
a WeChat message and I'd pick it up.

806
00:43:44,730 --> 00:43:45,570
Sorry to make you come all the way here.

807
00:43:45,570 --> 00:43:47,700
I was just on my way. Our department...

808
00:43:48,230 --> 00:43:48,960
is on the way.

809
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:51,090
Then, please have a seat.

810
00:43:51,090 --> 00:43:52,050
I'll go get you a glass of water.

811
00:43:52,050 --> 00:43:52,690
Okay.

812
00:43:57,570 --> 00:43:58,900
Aren't you busy lately?

813
00:43:59,010 --> 00:44:01,740
Not too bad.
Just processing some data and stuff.

814
00:44:05,090 --> 00:44:06,410
Have some water first.

815
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:09,560
I just noticed on my way up

816
00:44:09,710 --> 00:44:11,820
that your company really is all guys.

817
00:44:12,510 --> 00:44:13,210
Yeah.

818
00:44:13,920 --> 00:44:15,260
This industry, you know...

819
00:44:15,260 --> 00:44:17,690
Very few girls can handle it.

820
00:44:17,690 --> 00:44:19,690
You need to stay up late all the time.

821
00:44:20,300 --> 00:44:21,340
Wait a moment.

822
00:44:23,680 --> 00:44:26,380
Son, what do you think of this girl?

823
00:44:27,230 --> 00:44:29,690
Mom, can't you give me a break?

824
00:44:33,690 --> 00:44:35,730
How are your parents doing lately?

825
00:44:37,740 --> 00:44:39,420
They're doing well,

826
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:41,210
but a bit annoying recently.

827
00:44:41,210 --> 00:44:42,540
They keep messaging me.

828
00:44:42,570 --> 00:44:44,100
Rushing you to get married?

829
00:44:50,880 --> 00:44:52,180
Lin Zhixia...

830
00:44:53,610 --> 00:44:55,050
If you tell her anything,

831
00:44:55,050 --> 00:44:56,510
the whole world will know.

832
00:44:58,390 --> 00:45:00,960
Yeah, I've been pressured a lot lately.

833
00:45:01,920 --> 00:45:03,900
But our job is just like this.

834
00:45:03,900 --> 00:45:05,010
From day to night,

835
